              <zone h='100000' id='6' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
                <zone fixed-size='65' forceUpdate='true' h='9506' id='5' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='20'>Social Media </run>
                    <run fontsize='20'>Addiction Analysis</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8' italic='true'>Based on Data of 1M Users Aged 13 to 27</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone h='5469' id='67' type-v2='text' w='100000' x='0' y='9506'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run>Developed and Analyzed by: Tran Nguyen
Data Source: Kaggle.com</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='240' forceUpdate='true' h='32292' id='66' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='100000' x='0' y='14975'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontsize='11'>- The data includes 1 million users from 7 countries: Australia, Brazil, Canada, Germany, India, UK, and the US. Users are aged 13 to 27, a young demographic that is heavily active on social media.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>- The primary platforms in this analysis are five mainstream ones: Instagram, Snapchat, TikTok, Twitter (X), and YouTube. Based on the visualization,</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='11'> Instagram, YouTube, and TikTok </run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>are the top three most used primary platforms.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>- On average, users spend</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='11'> 3.5 hours </run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>a day on social media, and each session lasts approximately 25 minutes. This is consistent across all countries in the dataset.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>- Demographically, there is no difference across genders, ages, or countries in the number of platforms used, daily usage, screen time before sleep, or purpose of use. Roughly </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='11'>40%</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'> of users say they use social media for </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='11'>entertainment</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>, while Content Creation and News are the least common purposes.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>- </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Night usage makes no visible difference.</run>
                    <run fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> Users active late at night have essentially the same mental health scores as those who are not, within each addiction level. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>- The most notable difference is mental health score by addiction level. The gap between High and Low addiction is about 3</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='11'>.2 points </run>
                    <run fontsize='11'>(5.371 vs. 8.611). Medium addiction is the most common level on every platform, followed by Low and then High. Because most users fall into the Medium group, the overall average mental health score (7.17) sits close to the Medium score (7.042).</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='background-color' value='#304662' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <_.fcp.DashboardRoundedCorners.true...format attr='corner-radius' value='10' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
